<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia awards rail job to DRB, partners.</title>
<headline>Malaysia awards rail job to DRB, partners.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Malaysian government has awarded a 300 million ringgit railway project to two joint companies involving motor vehicle firm Diversified Resources Bhd (DRB), the national Bernama news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The agency quoted Transport Minister Ling Liong Sik as saying a consortium which groups DRB and Japan's Mitsui Co Ltd would carry out the costing and detailed engineering works related to the double-track rail project.</p>
<p>DRB and Italy's Fiat Ferroviaria SpA would jointly deliver seven sets of trains, Ling said.</p>
<p>The railway line will link northern Ipoh city to Rawang, an area just outside capital Kuala Lumpur.</p>
<p>Previous newspaper reports said the project is part of a government plan to upgrade the railway lines and trains.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
